# Model weights. `checkpoints/` is 2.0 GB of .pt files, far past what GitHub will take, and
# CLAUDE.md records that 88 of the 123 are stale 25-channel files that no longer even load
# against the current environment. They stay on the training machine.
#
# NOT TRACKED AND NOT REPLACEABLE - back these up by hand:
#   checkpoints/20260910-224257_iter200.pt   the original +2367-on-level2ProMax peak
#   checkpoints/20260911-114307_iter200.pt   the teacher behind the rank-288 submission
#
# What IS tracked is everything needed to rebuild an agent from one: the configs, the training
# code, `submission.py`, and the frozen bakes under `baselines/`.
checkpoints/

# Debug bakes. `bake_debug_agent.py` output is ~5 MB of fp16 weights and is regenerable in one
# command, so the script is tracked and its output is not. It is also NOT a submission: it carries
# the value head, which no submission ever should.
debug_submission.py

# Byte-compiled
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/

# Notebook scratch state (the notebooks themselves are tracked, outputs and all)
.ipynb_checkpoints/

# Per-machine Claude Code state: a permission allowlist and a task lock, useful to nobody else.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.lock

# Editor / OS noise
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.swp
